.TH COF-EJECT 1 "2026-11-13" "cof 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cof-eject \- Copy a bundled orchestration to the current directory for editing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cof eject [OPTIONS] {name}
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copies a bundled orchestration's own file into the current directory, for
local editing -- the bundled copy itself is never writable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B name
NAME Name of the orchestration to eject.
.TP
.B --out, -o
OUT Output path. Defaults to ./<filename>.
.TP
.B --config, -c
CONFIG Path to config JSON (or use CIRCUITRY_CONFIG).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cof eject hello-world
Copies the bundled hello-world.yml here.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, or the input was invalid.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error -- an unrecognized option or missing argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcof(1)\fR, \fBcof-info(1)\fR, \fBcof-run(1)\fR
